  "body": "**What changed:** `list_features` took a face's `normal` from the plane, which is sign-canonical (winding-independent) by design, so a cylinder's or box's bottom cap read `[0,0,1]` / \"up\". `outward()` in `crates/app/src/mcp/features.rs` now flips the normal to the side the face's summed facet winding points at; `facing` derives from it. Faces whose winding sums to nothing keep the canonical normal. The geometry crate (face ids) is untouched. `list_features` is the only tool reporting `facing`.\n\n**Root cause:** tool, not fixture - the fixture's winding is right.\n\n**Tests:** `list_features_facing_follows_the_outward_side` (cylinder boss + box: 1 up, 1 down, 4 side; bottom normal -Z) in `crates/app/tests/mcp_pick.rs`; `flat_face` helper there now picks by `facing`. Quick gate (`app lib`, `mcp_pick`, `mcp_setup` locate test) green; clippy `-D warnings` clean on camcraft-app. Not exercised: STEP import.\n\nEffort: medium\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\nChangelog: MCP `list_features` reports a downward-facing flat face as \"down\" with an outward normal (#884, PR #947)\n\nFixes #884\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
